    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Clustered heatmaps in Python with canvasxpress\"\ndescription: \"Build an interactive, clustered gene-expression heatmap with dendrograms and sample annotations from a DataFrame in Python — one portable, reproducible spec.\"\nauthor: \"Isaac Neuhaus\"\ndate: \"2026-09-24\"\ncategories: [Python, canvasxpress, heatmap, bioinformatics, visualization]\nimage: \"thumbnail.png\"\njupyter: python3\n---\n\n\nThe clustered heatmap is the default way to look at an expression matrix: rows and columns reordered\nby similarity, dendrograms on the margins, and sample metadata alongside. Here we build one in Python\nwith [canvasxpress](https://pypi.org/project/canvasxpress/) — clustering happens inside the render,\nso you pass a plain matrix and get an interactive, reproducible figure.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\npip install canvasxpress\n```\n\n## An expression matrix with sample metadata\n\nSwap this simulated block for your own matrix (genes in rows, samples in columns) and a table of\nper-sample annotations.\n\n::: {#573c5662 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nrng   = np.random.default_rng(1)\nng, ns = 40, 30\ngenes = [f\"Gene{i+1}\" for i in range(ng)]\nsamps = [f\"S{i+1}\"    for i in range(ns)]\ncond  = [\"Tumor\"] * (ns // 2) + [\"Normal\"] * (ns // 2)\n\nm = rng.normal(0, 1, (ng, ns))\ntumor = [i for i, c in enumerate(cond) if c == \"Tumor\"]\nnormal = [i for i, c in enumerate(cond) if c == \"Normal\"]\nm[np.ix_(range(0, 20),  tumor)]  += 2      # first block up in Tumor\nm[np.ix_(range(20, 40), normal)] += 2      # second block up in Normal\n\nexpr = pd.DataFrame(m.round(3), index=genes, columns=samps)\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Build the spec\n\nThe matrix goes in as `data`, and the sample annotation becomes an annotation track over the\ncolumns. `samplesClustered` / `variablesClustered` turn on hierarchical clustering with dendrograms.\n\n::: {#3a926301 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfrom canvasxpress.canvas import CanvasXpress\nfrom canvasxpress.render.jupyter import CXNoteBook\nfrom IPython.display import display\n\ndata = {\n    \"y\": {\"vars\": genes, \"smps\": samps, \"data\": expr.values.tolist()},\n    \"x\": {\"Condition\": cond},\n}\n\nconfig = {\n    \"graphType\": \"Heatmap\",\n    \"samplesClustered\": True, \"variablesClustered\": True,\n    \"colorSpectrum\": [\"navy\", \"white\", \"firebrick3\"],\n    \"showSmpDendrogram\": True, \"showVarDendrogram\": True,\n    \"title\": \"Clustered expression heatmap\",\n}\n\ncx = CanvasXpress(render_to=\"heatmap\", data=data, config=config, width=650, height=550)\nfor part in CXNoteBook(cx).render():\n    display(part)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(1, 1fr); gap: 10px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div><canvas id=\"heatmap\" width=650 height=550></canvas></div>\n</div>\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<script type=\"application/javascript\">\n\n// 1. First, handle CSS Insertion and wait for it to be completely ready\nnew Promise((cssResolve, cssReject) => {\n    const cssUrl = \"https://www.canvasxpress.org/dist/canvasXpress.css\";\n    let existingLink = document.querySelector(`head link[href=\"${cssUrl}\"]`);\n\n    if (!existingLink) {\n        const link = document.createElement(\"link\");\n        link.rel = \"stylesheet\";\n        link.type = \"text/css\";\n        link.href = cssUrl;\n        link.onload = () => {\n            link.dataset.state = \"loaded\";\n            link.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"assetLoaded\"));\n            cssResolve();\n        };\n        link.onerror = () => {\n            link.dataset.state = \"failed\";\n            link.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"assetFailed\"));\n            cssReject(new Error(`Failed to load CSS: ${cssUrl}`));\n        };\n        document.head.appendChild(link);\n    } else if (existingLink.dataset.state === \"loaded\") {\n        cssResolve();\n    } else if (existingLink.dataset.state === \"failed\") {\n        cssReject(new Error(`Failed to load CSS: ${cssUrl}`));\n    } else {\n        // Safe queueing for subsequent runs initiated while CSS is downloading\n        existingLink.addEventListener('assetLoaded', () => cssResolve(), { once: true });\n        existingLink.addEventListener('assetFailed', () => cssReject(new Error(`Failed to load CSS: ${cssUrl}`)), { once: true });\n    }\n})\n.then(() => {\n    // 2. CSS is guaranteed ready. Now handle JS Insertion\n    return new Promise((jsResolve, jsReject) => {\n        const scriptUrl = 'https://www.canvasxpress.org/dist/canvasXpress.min.js';\n        let existingScript = document.querySelector(`script[src=\"${scriptUrl}\"]`);\n\n        if (existingScript) {\n            if (existingScript.dataset.state === \"loaded\") {\n                jsResolve();\n            } else if (existingScript.dataset.state === \"failed\") {\n                jsReject(new Error(`Failed to load script: ${scriptUrl}`));\n            } else {\n                // Safe queueing for subsequent runs initiated while JS is downloading\n                existingScript.addEventListener('assetLoaded', () => jsResolve(), { once: true });\n                existingScript.addEventListener('assetFailed', () => jsReject(new Error(`Failed to load script: ${scriptUrl}`)), { once: true });\n            }\n        } else {\n            const script = document.createElement(\"script\");\n            script.type = \"text/javascript\";\n            script.src = scriptUrl;\n            script.dataset.state = \"loading\";\n\n            script.onload = () => {\n                script.dataset.state = \"loaded\";\n                script.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"assetLoaded\"));\n                jsResolve();\n            };\n            script.onerror = () => {\n                script.dataset.state = \"failed\";\n                script.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"assetFailed\"));\n                jsReject(new Error(`Failed to load script: ${scriptUrl}`));\n            };\n            document.head.appendChild(script);\n        }\n    });\n})\n.then(() => { \n    // 3. Both CSS and JS are ready in order. Run user payload.\n    \ntry {\n  // 1. Get the chart object using the HTML element ID\n  let myChart = CanvasXpress.getObject(\"heatmap\");\n  \n  // 2. Check if the chart exists before trying to delete it\n  if (myChart) {\n    myChart.destroy();\n    console.log(\"Chart heatmap removed for re-rendering.\");\n  } else {\n    console.log(\"Chart heatmap ready for rendering.\");\n  }\n} catch (error) {\n  // 3. Handle any unexpected errors safely\n  console.error(\"Chart heatmap could not be cleaned for re-rendering:\", error);\n}\n\nvar chart_heatmap = new CanvasXpress({\"renderTo\": \"heatmap\", \"data\": {\"y\": {\"vars\": [\"Gene1\", \"Gene2\", \"Gene3\", \"Gene4\", \"Gene5\", \"Gene6\", \"Gene7\", \"Gene8\", \"Gene9\", \"Gene10\", \"Gene11\", \"Gene12\", \"Gene13\", \"Gene14\", \"Gene15\", \"Gene16\", \"Gene17\", \"Gene18\", \"Gene19\", \"Gene20\", \"Gene21\", \"Gene22\", \"Gene23\", \"Gene24\", \"Gene25\", \"Gene26\", \"Gene27\", \"Gene28\", \"Gene29\", \"Gene30\", \"Gene31\", \"Gene32\", \"Gene33\", \"Gene34\", \"Gene35\", \"Gene36\", \"Gene37\", \"Gene38\", \"Gene39\", \"Gene40\"], \"smps\": [\"S1\", \"S2\", \"S3\", \"S4\", \"S5\", \"S6\", \"S7\", \"S8\", \"S9\", \"S10\", \"S11\", \"S12\", \"S13\", \"S14\", \"S15\", \"S16\", \"S17\", \"S18\", \"S19\", \"S20\", \"S21\", \"S22\", \"S23\", \"S24\", \"S25\", \"S26\", \"S27\", \"S28\", \"S29\", \"S30\"], \"data\": [[2.346, 2.822, 2.33, 0.697, 2.905, 2.446, 1.463, 2.581, 2.365, 2.294, 2.028, 2.547, 1.264, 1.837, 1.518, 0.599, 0.04, -0.292, -0.782, -0.257, 0.008, -0.276, 1.294, 1.007, -2.711, -1.889, -0.175, -0.422, 0.214, 0.217], [4.118, 0.888, 1.622, 4.043, 2.647, 2.663, 1.486, 0.352, 2.167, 2.109, 0.773, 1.317